{:edb/db-before-t 1227 :edb/db-after-t 1228 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534540 50 #inst "2026-10-07T21:24:21.119Z" 13194139534540 true] [17592186087639 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293811 13194139534540 true] [17592186087640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293804 13194139534540 true] [17592186087640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293818 13194139534540 true] [17592186087640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293822 13194139534540 true] [17592186087928 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534540 true] [17592186087928 1100 "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534540 true] [17592186087928 1100 "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139534540 false] [17592186087928 1145 "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 1=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 0-0\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible. Since $C$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $C$ is singular.\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is singular." 13194139534540 true] [17592186293804 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293805 13194139534540 true] [17592186293804 1089 "q-11721" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293804 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534540 true] [17592186293804 1100 "If $Q=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ x & x\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293804 1113 #uuid "62137868-7223-57f4-91c5-f73e65369a0e" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293804 1145 "The matrix $Q$ is singular if and only if $det(Q)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =3\\cdot x-x\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3x-6x \\\\  & =-3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $x$ is $x=0.$" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293805 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293806 13194139534540 true] [17592186293805 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293807 13194139534540 true] [17592186293805 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293808 13194139534540 true] [17592186293805 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293809 13194139534540 true] [17592186293805 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293810 13194139534540 true] [17592186293805 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534540 true] [17592186293805 1041 "selection" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293805 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293807 13194139534540 true] [17592186293805 1110 #uuid "ad7c601f-504d-5f29-b9cb-02750eaaed08" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293806 1034 "x=2" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293806 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534540 true] [17592186293806 1111 #uuid "e38e2950-b33d-57e2-ac54-303fa190d88b" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293807 1034 "x=0" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293807 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534540 true] [17592186293807 1111 #uuid "dedd7c41-6862-5d00-9cc7-35fd026d3c9e" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293808 1034 "x=\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293808 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534540 true] [17592186293808 1111 #uuid "4961011c-5cfc-5a70-9553-cb8662177cca" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293809 1034 "x=-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293809 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534540 true] [17592186293809 1111 #uuid "72091842-7dda-5fe5-9f45-c59b698a6daa" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293810 1034 "x=-2" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293810 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534540 true] [17592186293810 1111 #uuid "93175766-554d-5f98-995c-8a8465cf6ff8" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293811 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293812 13194139534540 true] [17592186293811 1089 "q-127762" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293811 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534540 true] [17592186293811 1100 "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 12 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293811 1113 #uuid "37527fee-ef2e-503d-b544-20319e41e15b" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293811 1145 "- The matrix $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=4\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 3=2.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=4\\cdot 9-3\\cdot 12=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ do not have an inverse." 13194139534540 true] [17592186293812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293813 13194139534540 true] [17592186293812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293814 13194139534540 true] [17592186293812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293815 13194139534540 true] [17592186293812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293816 13194139534540 true] [17592186293812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293817 13194139534540 true] [17592186293812 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534540 true] [17592186293812 1041 "selection" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293812 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293813 13194139534540 true] [17592186293812 1110 #uuid "7d244270-8b63-5656-8fa2-5e415614be7a" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293813 1034 "$A$ and $C$ only" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293813 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534540 true] [17592186293813 1111 #uuid "467d76df-1d50-5b9c-8869-a83fa9eccf2f" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293814 1034 "$B$ and $C$ only" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293814 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534540 true] [17592186293814 1111 #uuid "f9d6119f-9517-593b-9834-38494d8d00af" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293815 1034 "$A$ and $B$ only" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293815 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534540 true] [17592186293815 1111 #uuid "cbc018ff-03c6-5810-ae51-3b027c1419df" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293816 1034 "$C$ only" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293816 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534540 true] [17592186293816 1111 #uuid "34579017-7361-5dc4-a5fe-28c2f6510e66" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293817 1034 "$B$ only" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293817 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534540 true] [17592186293817 1111 #uuid "2ca1bd59-4484-5b5e-ad7b-e319cc4eec55" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293818 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293819 13194139534540 true] [17592186293818 1089 "q-316782" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293818 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534540 true] [17592186293818 1100 "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3x+2 & 2x-4\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293818 1113 #uuid "0047a425-3434-51cf-8bea-b68dedd67cd7" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293818 1145 "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =1\\cdot (2x-4)-2\\cdot (3x+2) \\\\  & =2x-4-6x-4 \\\\  & =-4x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x-8 & =0 \\\\ -4x & =8 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293820 13194139534540 true] [17592186293819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293821 13194139534540 true] [17592186293819 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534540 true] [17592186293819 1041 "field-1" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293819 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293821 13194139534540 true] [17592186293819 1110 #uuid "88f236f3-feef-563d-a98b-ee60e0ff782a" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293820 1034 "2" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293820 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534540 true] [17592186293820 1111 #uuid "b143ed6d-3f8a-5a5f-9b22-6a3acb7a18ab" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293821 1034 "-2" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293821 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534540 true] [17592186293821 1111 #uuid "b0d1eee9-040f-510d-b5a6-b707a05db1ec" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293822 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293823 13194139534540 true] [17592186293822 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293825 13194139534540 true] [17592186293822 1089 "q-316825" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293822 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534540 true] [17592186293822 1100 "Let $B=[\\begin{aligned}2x+4 & 0 \\\\ 15 & -x-3\\end{aligned}]$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534540 true] [17592186293822 1113 #uuid "877694df-7d13-5599-a77e-7aa2ec2835a6" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293822 1145 "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x+4)\\cdot (-x-3)-0\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-6x-4x-12 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-10x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-10x-12 & =0 \\\\ -2({x}^{2}+5x+6) & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,x=-2.\n$$" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293823 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293824 13194139534540 true] [17592186293823 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534540 true] [17592186293823 1041 "field-1" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293823 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293824 13194139534540 true] [17592186293823 1110 #uuid "dcba2a08-0178-52dc-b69b-1958b893f397" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293824 1034 "-3" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293824 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534540 true] [17592186293824 1111 #uuid "f49a3a5a-a1bf-5a07-8daf-be24ac11f73b" 13194139534540 true] [17592186293825 1000 #edb/ref 1759